al Cities Tour</h1><p class='lead'>Discover Morocco’s historical treasures from Casablanca to Marrakech through this cultural journey that highlights imperial cities, ancient ruins, and royal landmarks.</p><div class='et-ctas'><a class='et-btn' href='#et-iti'>See the day-by-day plan <svg aria-hidden='true' width='16' height='16'><use href='#et-i-arrow'/></svg></a><a class='et-btn et-btn-w et-btn-wa' href='https://wa.me/212661292596?text=Hello%20Epic%20Travel%20Morocco,%20I%20am%20interested%20in%20the%20Moroccan%20Historical%20Cities%20Tour%20(8%20days).%20' target='_blank' rel='noopener'><svg aria-hidden='true'><use href='#et-i-wa'/></svg>Book on WhatsApp</a></div></div></section><div class='et'><div class='et-wrap'><div class='et-facts'><div><b>8 days</b><span>7 nights</span></div><div><b>Casablanca</b><span>starting point</span></div><div><b>Casablanca</b><span>end of the tour</span></div><div><b>Private</b><span>your own driver &amp; vehicle</span></div></div></div></div><section class='et et-sec' id='et-iti'><div class='et-wrap et-tour'><div><h3 style='font-size:20px'>Route</h3><div class='et-stops'><span>Casablanca</span><span>Rabat</span><span>Meknes</span><span>Fes</span><span>Volubilis</span><span>Moulay Idriss</span><span>Beni Mellal</span><span>Marrakech</span></div><div class='et-iti-h'><div><span class='et-eye'>Itinerary</span><h2>Day by day</h2></div><button type='button' class='et-tog' data-o='0'>Open all days</button></div><div class='et-iti'><details class='et-day et-rv' open><summary><span class='et-node'>1</span><small>Day 1</small><b>Casablanca</b></summary><div class='et-day-b'><p>Pick up at the Casablanca airport and transfer to your hotel.</p><h4>Hassan II Mosque</h4><p>You can start your day visiting the famous Hassan II Mosque, the largest religious building in the world open to non-Muslims. Its magnificent design combines modern engineering and traditional Moroccan craftsmanship.</p><h4>Old Medina</h4><p>Walk through the souk in the old medina, passing Bab Marrakech and its charming small hotels built during the protectorate. Discover the authentic daily life of locals.</p><h4>United Nations Square</h4><p>A vibrant hub connecting the old and modern parts of Casablanca — surrounded by shops, cafés, and historic hotels like Hyatt Regency.</p><h4>The Corniche & Morocco Mall</h4><p>Visit the seaside promenade of Ain Diab, filled with cafés, beaches, and the Morocco Mall — Africa’s second-largest shopping center.</p></div></details><details class='et-day et-rv'><summary><span class='et-node'>2</span><small>Day 2</small><b>Casablanca · Rabat</b></summary><div class='et-day-b'><p>After breakfast, depart to Rabat — Morocco’s political and administrative capital.</p><p>Visit the Kasbah of the Udayas, the Mausoleum of Mohammed V, and the impressive Hassan Tower. Stroll through the Andalusian Gardens and the charming medina filled with artisan shops.</p><p>Explore the Chellah Necropolis, an ancient Roman site later used as a royal burial ground. Overnight stay in Rabat.</p></div></details><details class='et-day et-rv'><summary><span class='et-node'>3</span><small>Day 3</small><b>Rabat · Meknes · Fes</b></summary><div class='et-day-b'><p>After breakfast, drive to Meknes, one of Morocco’s imperial cities. Begin your visit at Bab Mansour, the grand gate facing El Hedim Square. Explore the Dar Jamaï Museum, showcasing traditional Moroccan arts, woodwork, and ceramics.</p><p>Later, continue to Fes, the country’s oldest imperial city, and check in at your traditional riad.</p></div></details><details class='et-day et-rv'><summary><span class='et-node'>4</span><small>Day 4</small><b>Fes · Moulay Idriss · Volubilis</b></summary><div class='et-day-b'><p>Depart for a two-hour drive to explore Volubilis, Morocco’s most famous Roman ruins and a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Discover ancient mosaics, temples, and arches that tell the story of Roman civilization in North Africa.</p><p>Continue to the holy town of Moulay Idriss, beautifully perched on twin hills, and enjoy panoramic views. Return to Fes for dinner and overnight stay.</p></div></details><details class='et-day et-rv'><summary><span class='et-node'>5</span><small>Day 5</small><b>Explore Fes</b></summary><div class='et-day-b'><p>After breakfast, begin a full-day guided tour of Fes, Morocco’s cultural and spiritual heart.</p><p>Visit the Bou Inania Madrasa, Kairaouine Mosque and University, Nejjarine Fountain, and the famous tanneries. Explore the Jewish quarter (Mellah) and see the coexistence of different communities.</p><p>Discover key sites such as:</p><ul><li>Medersa Bou Inania</li><li>University of Al Karaouine</li><li>Medersa el Attarin</li><li>Zaouia Moulay Idriss II</li><li>Dar Batha Museum</li></ul><p>Spend the evening relaxing in your riad or exploring the medina at leisure.</p></div></details><details class='et-day et-rv'><summary><span class='et-node'>6</span><small>Day 6</small><b>Fes · Beni Mellal · Marrakech</b></summary><div class='et-day-b'><p>Travel through the Middle Atlas Mountains toward Beni Mellal, surrounded by olive and orange groves. Stop for a traditional Berber lunch and explore the area’s scenic waterfalls and old kasbahs.</p><p>Continue through Kasba Tadla, a garrison town built by Moulay Ismail in the 17th century, before arriving in Marrakech in the evening. Overnight stay in Marrakech.</p></div></details><details class='et-day et-rv'><summary><span class='et-node'>7</span><small>Day 7</small><b>Tour of Marrakech</b></summary><div class='et-day-b'><p>Discover Marrakech, the “Red City,” starting with the Koutoubia Mosque and the vibrant Jemaa El Fna square. Wander through the souks filled with carpets, spices, jewelry, and crafts.</p><p>Visit:</p><ul><li>Saadian Tombs</li><li>El Badii Palace</li><li>Bahia Palace</li><li>Mellah (Jewish Quarter)</li><li>Majorelle Gardens</li></ul><p>Enjoy a delicious lunch and conclude the evening with the Chez Ali Fantasia dinner show before returning to your riad.</p></div></details><details class='et-day et-rv'><summary><span class='et-node'>8</span><small>Day 8</small><b>Marrakech · Casablanca</b></summary><div class='et-day-b'><p>After breakfast, transfer back to Casablanca for your departure flight.<br>Your Morocco Historical Cities Tour comes to an end — with unforgettable memories and experiences.</p></div></details></div><div class='et-note'><svg aria-hidden='true'><use href='#et-i-info'/></svg><div><b>Tailor-made:</b> Every itinerary can be adapted — start date, number of days, hotels and stops. Tell us your dates and we send you a detailed quote.</div></div></div><aside class='et-side'><div class='et-book'><div class='et-book-h et-dark'><h3>Book this tour</h3><p>Free quote within 24 hours — no payment to ask.</p></div><ul><li><span>Duration</span><b>8 days / 7 nights</b></li><li><span>Start</span><b>Casablanca</b></li><li><span>End</span><b>Casablanca</b></li><li><span>Style</span><b>Imperial cities</b></li><li><span>Type</span><b>Private tour</b></li></ul><div class='et-book-f'><a class='et-btn et-btn-wa' href='https://wa.me/212661292596?text=Hello%20Epic%20Travel%20Morocco,%20I%20am%20interested%20in%20the%20Moroccan%20Historical%20Cities%20Tour%20(8%20days).%20' target='_blank' rel='noopener'><svg aria-hidden='true'><use href='#et-i-wa'/></svg>Book on WhatsApp</a><a class='et-btn et-btn-o' href='mailto:epictravelmorocco@gmail.com?subject=Moroccan%20Historical%20Cities%20Tour'><svg aria-hidden='true'><use href='#et-i-mail'/></svg>Email us</a><a class='et-btn' href='https://epictravelmorocco.com/contact-2/'>Send a request</a><small>WhatsApp +212 661 292 596 · Tel +1 579 484 7707</small></div></div></aside></div></section><section class='et et-sec et-pat'><div class='et-wrap'><div class='et-head'><div class='et-orn'><svg aria-hidden='true'><use href='#et-i-star'/></svg></div><span class='et-eye'>You may also like</span><h2>More Morocco tours</h2></div><div class='et-grid'><a class='et-card et-rv' href='https://epic